<title>UK: Granada plans 40 mln stg hotel sale - paper.</title>
<headline>Granada plans 40 mln stg hotel sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Granada Plc, the British hotels and leisure group, is expected to sell its Plaza Athenee hotel in Paris for more than 40 million sterling, Britain's Sunday Times newspaper said.</p>
<p>The hotel sale, expected to be made to the younger brother of the Sultan of Brunei, Prince Jefri Bolkiah, will bring the aggregate value of disposals by Granada since it took over Forte to 1.2 billion sterling, the paper said.</p>
